Module 1: The Biomimetic Skin Interface (UGIRAP Gecko Patch)
 * What it does: Secures the wearable artificial kidney to the patient's skin securely without chemical glues, irritation, or skin tearing.
 * How it works: Inspired by gecko foot geometry, the patch features millions of microscopic flexible stalks (setae) terminating in sub-micron pads (spatulae). These structures conform to the microscopic ridges of the skin, generating strong dry van der Waals physical adhesion (\ge 5.2\text{ N/cm}^2).
 * Sweat Management: Interspersed capillary microchannels (10\text{ to }50\ \mu\text{m} diameter) continuously wick sweat away from the contact boundary into a perimeter hydrogel ring, preventing skin maceration during continuous 72-hour wear cycles. Peeling the patch at a 45-degree directional angle collapses the contact geometry for pain-free removal.
Module 2: The Hemofiltration Core (Silicon Nanopore Membrane)
 * What it does: Filters uremic toxins (urea, creatinine, middle molecules) out of the fluid stream while retaining vital blood proteins like albumin.
 * How it works: Utilizes a single-crystal silicon nanopore membrane (SNM) etched with uniform 5 to 7 nm rectangular slit pores that mimic the podocyte slit diaphragms of human renal glomeruli.
 * Non-Thrombogenic Coating: All fluid-contacting surfaces are covalently modified with an ultrathin (sub-5 nm) zwitterionic poly(sulfobetaine methacrylate) (pSBMA) hydrogel monolayer. This layer forms a permanent electrostatic hydration barrier that prevents protein adsorption and blood clotting without requiring continuous systemic blood thinners (heparin-free).
Module 3: Active Self-Cleaning (Piezo-Acoustic & Magnetic Defouling)
 * What it does: Prevents protein cake accumulation from clogging the silicon nanopore filter over extended operational wear.
 * How it works (Acoustic): Thin-film Aluminum Nitride (AlN) piezoelectric transducers project Surface Acoustic Waves (SAWs) across the membrane using the Dual-Frequency Interleaved Phase-Shifted Sweep (DF-IPSS) protocol (40\text{ to }100\text{ kHz}). Acoustic micro-vortices sweep accumulated protein layers off the zwitterionic surface. Acoustic intensity is capped strictly below 0.25\text{ W/cm}^2 to prevent red blood cell damage (hemolysis), operating on a 15\text{ ms} pulse / 85\text{ ms} rest duty cycle.
 * Physical Fallback (Magnetic Wiper): A zwitterionic-coated micro-wiper containing embedded superparamagnetic nanoparticles rests inside the fluid chamber. An external magnetic actuator translates a localized magnetic field to drag the scraper across the membrane, physically clearing stubborn protein deposits without breaking the sterile fluid seal.
Module 4: The Gas-Sublimation Reactor (Photoelectrocatalytic PEC Cell)
 * What it does: Eliminates the daily physiological urea load (15\text{ to }25\text{ g/day}) without requiring heavy 120-liter water tanks or enzymatic urease sorbents.
 * How it works: Filtrate enters a microfluidic photoelectrocatalytic flow cell containing a nanostructured hematite photoanode coated with a nickel oxyhydroxide (NiOOH) catalyst. Illuminated by continuous 460 nm blue micro-LEDs, the cell oxidizes urea directly into harmless nitrogen (N_2) and carbon dioxide (CO_2) gases:
The evolved gases vent safely into ambient air through hydrophobic expanded polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) membranes.
Module 5: Living Cell Bioreactor & Deterministic Brain
 * Proximal Tubule Bioreactor: Filtered fluid passes through a cell culture chamber housing conditionally immortalized human proximal tubule epithelial cells (RPTEC/TERT1). Subjected to continuous fluid shear stress (0.2\text{ to }0.5\text{ dyne/cm}^2), these cells form polarized 3D tubular structures that actively reabsorb essential electrolytes (sodium, potassium, bicarbonate) and glucose back into circulation.
 * The Deterministic Brain (ce_os): System operations are monitored by the ce_os kernel written in bare-metal, no_std Rust running on a 32-bit RISC-V microcontroller. Operating on a hard real-time 10 ms control loop with zero dynamic memory allocation, ce_os continuously tracks pressure, acoustic power, and optical fluid leak detectors. If air bubbles or pressure surges occur, the safety firewall actuates an electromagnetic bypass valve within 9.15\text{ ns} using Rayleigh cavitation collapse logic, isolating the patient loop safely.
